{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UePeYn8smsfg2rvXZzPWtb","type":"tool_result","content":"# Ticket #4471: no session replays since the redesign\n\nReported by product, 2026-10-16.\n\nReplay tab in PostHog shows sessions only from users still on the old UI\n(the A/B group). Users on the new UI appear in Events (screens, taps,\n`loan_amount_changed`, `application_submitted` all arrive) but have no\nrecording. Project settings: Record user sessions = on, sampling 100%,\nminimum duration 0. Same posthog_flutter version for both groups, same build.\nREADME.md\nSUPPORT-TICKET.md\nanalysis_options.yaml\nlib/analytics.dart\nlib/legacy_app.dart\nlib/main.dart\nlib/new_app.dart\nlib/screens/application_screen.dart\nlib/screens/calculator_screen.dart\nlib/screens/offers_screen.dart\nnotes/badges-for-your-users-achievements.md\nnotes/collecting-leads-with-apps-script.md\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md\npubspec.yaml\npubspec.yaml:13:  posthog_flutter: ^5.36.0\nREADME.md:9:Analytics: PostHog (`posthog_flutter`). Events, screen tracking and session\nREADME.md:11:the PostHog project settings, sampling 100%.\nSUPPORT-TICKET.md:5:Replay tab in PostHog shows sessions only from users still on the old UI\nSUPPORT-TICKET.md:9:minimum duration 0. Same posthog_flutter version for both groups, same build.\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:3:# PostHog session replay not working in Flutter? Add PostHogWidget\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:5:PostHog can record videos of real user sessions, so you can watch where people\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:10:Here is what we had: the `posthog_flutter` SDK set up, \"Record user sessions\"\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:13:`PosthogObserver` on the router. Every checklist item we could find was ticked.\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:14:PostHog's troubleshooting page covers sampling, retention and disabled\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:17:So I guessed. I changed settings in the PostHog console. I initialized the SDK\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:22:PostHog support gave us the answer. On mobile, Flutter replay is built from\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:24:`PostHogWidget`. If it doesn't wrap your `MaterialApp`, the SDK still records\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:38:Read-only. Preconditions: a Flutter app that depends on `posthog_flutter` and\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:40:1. `grep -rn \"posthog_flutter\" pubspec.yaml` — the package must be there.\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:43:3. `grep -rn \"MaterialApp\" lib/` and `grep -rn \"PostHogWidget\" lib/`.\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:45:in production is not inside a `PostHogWidget`.\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:49:[posthog_flutter](https://pub.dev/packages/posthog_flutter) >= 5.14.0\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:50:initialized via `Posthog().setup(config)`; a PostHog project with Session\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:59:2. Wrap each one: `return PostHogWidget(child: MaterialApp(...));`\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:60:   (import `package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart`). Add a comment\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:63:   `Posthog().setup(config)`, or call `Posthog().startSessionRecording()`\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:65:4. Keep `PosthogObserver()` in `navigatorObservers` (or the router's\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:70:differently and goes through posthog-js), move through 3–4 screens, then put\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:71:the app in the background so it flushes. Within a few minutes, Po