{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TqifzMFQp2AqPa7Xajs2TZ","type":"tool_result","content":"import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:go_router/go_router.dart';\nimport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\nimport 'screens/calculator_screen.dart';\nimport 'screens/application_screen.dart';\nimport 'screens/offers_screen.dart';\n\nfinal _router = GoRouter(\n  observers: [PosthogObserver()],\n  routes: [\n    GoRoute(path: '/', builder: (_, __) => const CalculatorScreen()),\n    GoRoute(path: '/apply', builder: (_, __) => const ApplicationScreen()),\n    GoRoute(path: '/offers', builder: (_, __) => const OffersScreen()),\n  ],\n);\n\n/// The redesigned shell (default since 2.3.0).\nclass NewApp extends StatelessWidget {\n  const NewApp({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return MaterialApp.router(\n      title: 'Loanly',\n      theme: ThemeData(\n        colorSchemeSeed: Colors.indigo,\n        useMaterial3: true,\n      ),\n      routerConfig: _router,\n    );\n  }\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\nimport 'screens/calculator_screen.dart';\nimport 'screens/application_screen.dart';\n\n/// The old shell. Kept for the A/B group until the redesign is fully rolled out.\nclass LegacyApp extends StatelessWidget {\n  const LegacyApp({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return PostHogWidget(\n      child: MaterialApp(\n        title: 'Loanly',\n        theme: ThemeData(colorSchemeSeed: Colors.teal),\n        navigatorObservers: [PosthogObserver()],\n        routes: {\n          '/': (_) => const CalculatorScreen(),\n          '/apply': (_) => const ApplicationScreen(),\n        },\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\nimport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\nclass Analytics {\n  static Future<void> init() async {\n    final config = PostHogConfig('phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI');\n    config.host = 'https://eu.i.posthog.com';\n    config.captureApplicationLifecycleEvents = true;\n    config.sessionReplay = true;\n    config.sessionReplayConfig.maskAllTexts = true;\n    config.sessionReplayConfig.maskAllImages = false;\n    await Posthog().setup(config);\n  }\n\n  static Future<void> track(String event, [Map<String, Object>? props]) =>\n      Posthog().capture(eventName: event, properties: props);\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nimport 'analytics.dart';\nimport 'legacy_app.dart';\nimport 'new_app.dart';\n\nconst bool useNewUi = bool.fromEnvironment('NEW_UI', defaultValue: true);\n\nFuture<void> main() async {\n  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();\n  await Analytics.init();\n  runApp(useNewUi ? const NewApp() : const LegacyApp());\n}\ninitialized via `Posthog().setup(config)`; a PostHog project with Session\nReplay enabled (Project settings → Session Replay → Record user sessions).\n\nYour agent will need from you: which entry point(s) and app widget(s) ship to\nusers; a device or emulator to run on.\n\nSteps:\n1. Find every root app widget (`MaterialApp`, `MaterialApp.router`,\n   `CupertinoApp`).\n2. Wrap each one: `return PostHogWidget(child: MaterialApp(...));`\n   (import `package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart`). Add a comment\n   saying replay needs it, so nobody removes it later.\n3. Make sure recording actually starts: `config.sessionReplay = true` before\n   `Posthog().setup(config)`, or call `Posthog().startSessionRecording()`\n   after setup if you gate it (feature flag, consent).\n4. Keep `PosthogObserver()` in `navigatorObservers` (or the router's\n   `observers`) so replays are split by screen.\n5. Optional, for PII: `config.sessionReplayConfig.maskAllTexts = true`.\n\nVerify: run a build on a real device or emulator (replay on web works\ndifferently and goes through posthog-js), move through 3–4 screens, then put","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6cc27fe4-7b29-4a0